@startuml
hide empty description
state "PASSIVE CONFIG / STARTUP\n(no device commands)" as PASSIVE
state "Cycle dispatch" as DISPATCH <<choice>>
state SAFE_STATE
state STOP_HOLD
state MANUAL_FIXED_CHARGE
state MANUAL_FIXED_DISCHARGE
state NIGHT_DISCHARGE
state HOLD
state CHARGE
state CHARGE_RAMP_DOWN
state DISCHARGE
state DISCHARGE_RAMP_DOWN

[*] --> PASSIVE
PASSIVE --> DISPATCH : control_allowed
DISPATCH --> PASSIVE : !control_allowed
DISPATCH --> SAFE_STATE : required data/command/runtime safety fault
DISPATCH --> STOP_HOLD : manual STOP
DISPATCH --> MANUAL_FIXED_CHARGE : manual fixed charge + allowed by SOC
DISPATCH --> MANUAL_FIXED_DISCHARGE : manual fixed discharge + allowed by SOC
DISPATCH --> NIGHT_DISCHARGE : night window + SOC above effective stop
DISPATCH --> HOLD : MIN/MAX_SOC or deadband/hold condition
DISPATCH --> CHARGE : AUTO export / Harvest-driven charge
DISPATCH --> DISCHARGE : AUTO import

CHARGE --> CHARGE_RAMP_DOWN : target must move toward 0 before stop/reversal
CHARGE_RAMP_DOWN --> HOLD : reaches 0
DISCHARGE --> DISCHARGE_RAMP_DOWN : target must move toward 0 before reversal
DISCHARGE_RAMP_DOWN --> HOLD : reaches 0

SAFE_STATE --> DISPATCH : next cycle; re-evaluate from fresh state
STOP_HOLD --> DISPATCH : next cycle
MANUAL_FIXED_CHARGE --> DISPATCH : next cycle / target-SOC completion
MANUAL_FIXED_DISCHARGE --> DISPATCH : next cycle / target-SOC completion
NIGHT_DISCHARGE --> DISPATCH : next cycle; reserve/window exit actively neutralizes as needed
HOLD --> DISPATCH : next cycle
CHARGE --> DISPATCH : next cycle
DISCHARGE --> DISPATCH : next cycle

note right of DISPATCH
Priority within run_once():
control gate -> MQTT safety -> Manual -> Night ->
AUTO SOC/Grid -> Harvest update -> Cross-Charge existing target ->
Fast reversal guard -> Deadband / Import / Export.
end note
note bottom of CHARGE
Orthogonal layers, not current_mode states:
Harvest selects/modifies charge baseline.
Fast Capture overlays O on baseline B.
Cross-Charge can reduce the signed target toward 0.
end note
@enduml
